    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Apply high-level deformation intent using existing edit/algo capabilities.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  apply                       Apply stretch, corner-pin (video/sticker), or surface-track\r\n                              deformation.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft project create --ref local://example\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft project focus --ref local://example\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft config --ref local://example --ratio 16:9\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video add --ref local://example --resource local:///xx/yy/test.mp4\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft extract summary --ref local://example\r\n\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft --ref local://example --action video alpha --seg-id v1 --alpha 80% --action text style --seg-id t1 --color '#FFFFFF'\r\n\r\nACTION CHAINING\r\n  Same object, shared target:\r\n    lyra-cli draft video --seg-id v1 --action alpha --alpha 80% --action scale --scale 1.2\r\n  Same object, per-block targets:\r\n    lyra-cli draft video --action alpha --seg-id v1 --alpha 80% --action scale --seg-id v2 --scale 1.2\r\n  Cross object, per-block targets:\r\n    lyra-cli draft --action video alpha --seg-id v1 --alpha 80% --action text style --seg-id t1 --color '#FFFFFF'\r\n  Public selectors:\r\n    --seg-id, --seg-type, --target-track, --seg-index, --time-window\r\n  Shared and per-block targets cannot be mixed. Shortcut paths use spaces, not dots.\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  Use `lyra-cli draft <subcommand> --help` for more information.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Apply high-level deformation intent using existing edit/algo capabilities.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  apply                       Apply stretch, corner-pin (video/sticker), or surface-track\r\n                              deformation.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft project create --ref local://example\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft project focus --ref local://example\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft config --ref local://example --ratio 16:9\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video add --ref local://example --resource local:///xx/yy/test.mp4\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft extract summary --ref local://example\r\n\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft --ref local://example --action video alpha --seg-id v1 --alpha 80% --action text style --seg-id t1 --color '#FFFFFF'\r\n\r\nACTION CHAINING\r\n  Same object, shared target:\r\n    lyra-cli draft video --seg-id v1 --action alpha --alpha 80% --action scale --scale 1.2\r\n  Same object, per-block targets:\r\n    lyra-cli draft video --action alpha --seg-id v1 --alpha 80% --action scale --seg-id v2 --scale 1.2\r\n  Cross object, per-block targets:\r\n    lyra-cli draft --action video alpha --seg-id v1 --alpha 80% --action text style --seg-id t1 --color '#FFFFFF'\r\n  Public selectors:\r\n    --seg-id, --seg-type, --target-track, --seg-index, --time-window\r\n  Shared and per-block targets cannot be mixed. Shortcut paths use spaces, not dots.\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  Use `lyra